":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Single-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8129) - Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 7 265K (20 threads) - 31.37 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWith grid snapping enabled, the polygon 2d editor does not respect grid alignment. Creating or moving a vertex does not cleanly snap it to the grid point reliably. Clicking an existing vertex will cause it's alignment to shift around _near_ to the grid point, but can take many clicks to get it to be correctly on the point.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a polygon2d\n2. In polygon editor, enable grid & grid snapping\n3. Draw a set of vertexes. Observe their placement.\n4. Move vertexes. Observer their placement.\n5. Click on a vertex. Observe it's movement.\n6. Repeat 5 multiple times, behavior repeats.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"Use